## types

- analytic DE = DEM = true DE
- Claude DE = fake DE ( FDE): FDE=1/(g\*log(2)) when g>0 and undefined when g=0 (i.e., in interior)[\[4\]](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Fractals/Iterations_in_the_complex_plane/demm#cite_note-4)

## Math formule

Math formula:[\[5\]](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Fractals/Iterations_in_the_complex_plane/demm#cite_note-5)[\[6\]](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Fractals/Iterations_in_the_complex_plane/demm#cite_note-6)[\[7\]](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Fractals/Iterations_in_the_complex_plane/demm#cite_note-7)

distance(c0,σM)=limn→∞2\|zn\|\|zn′\|ln⁡\|zn\|{\\displaystyle distance(c\_{0},\\sigma M)=\\lim \_{n\\to \\infty }2{\\frac {\|z\_{n}\|}{\|z'\_{n}\|}}\\ln \|z\_{n}\|}![{\displaystyle distance(c_{0},\sigma M)=\lim _{n\to \infty }2{\frac {|z_{n}|}{|z'_{n}|}}\ln |z_{n}|}](https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/4874b89e28b3cf2a3fc8b18508b77ff671ceb837)

where:

zn=fcn(z=0.0){\\displaystyle z\_{n}=f\_{c}^{n}(z=0.0)}![{\displaystyle z_{n}=f_{c}^{n}(z=0.0)}](https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/ad07f1da773e8ec2db7f33ce490630209c435eb9)zn′=ddcfcn(z0).{\\displaystyle z\_{n}'={\\frac {d}{dc}}f\_{c}^{n}(z\_{0}).}![{\displaystyle z_{n}'={\frac {d}{dc}}f_{c}^{n}(z_{0}).}](https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/48a1bdef3c7e13b5fa43652a2d0d8c2fc4544403)

is a first [derivative](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Fractals/Mathematics/Derivative "Fractals/Mathematics/Derivative") of fcn(z0){\\displaystyle f\_{c}^{n}(z\_{0})}![{\displaystyle f_{c}^{n}(z_{0})}](https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/d01c2c37107471d460a7f5da7a89933a8c7a3489) with respect to _c_ which can be found by iteration starting with

z0′=ddcfc0(z0)=1{\\displaystyle z\_{0}'={\\frac {d}{dc}}f\_{c}^{0}(z\_{0})=1}![{\displaystyle z_{0}'={\frac {d}{dc}}f_{c}^{0}(z_{0})=1}](https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/3009cabb1ddc73ff6666bb307ccecd815ab4d79d)

and then replacing at every consecutive step

zn+1′=ddcfcn+1(z0)=2⋅fcn(z)⋅ddcfcn(z0)+1=2⋅zn⋅zn′+1.{\\displaystyle z\_{n+1}'={\\frac {d}{dc}}f\_{c}^{n+1}(z\_{0})=2\\cdot {}f\_{c}^{n}(z)\\cdot {\\frac {d}{dc}}f\_{c}^{n}(z\_{0})+1=2\\cdot z\_{n}\\cdot z\_{n}'+1.}![{\displaystyle z_{n+1}'={\frac {d}{dc}}f_{c}^{n+1}(z_{0})=2\cdot {}f_{c}^{n}(z)\cdot {\frac {d}{dc}}f_{c}^{n}(z_{0})+1=2\cdot z_{n}\cdot z_{n}'+1.}](https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/5bd8abd572cb2b45106115a73604e34dc79c3c03)

## Escape radius

- "you need to change "If mag > 2" to increase the escape radius. Attached is a comparison, showing that the "straps" reduce when the radius is increased, no harm going huge like R = 1e6 or so because once it escapes 2 it grows very fast. The bigger the radius, the more accurate the distance estimate." Claude [\[8\]](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Fractals/Iterations_in_the_complex_plane/demm#cite_note-8)
- Basically in testing magnitude squared against bailout
  - if your bailout is 10^4 then your DE estimates are accurate to 2 decimal figures i.e. if your DE is 0.01 then it's only accurate to +/-0.0001,
  - if your bailout is 10^6 then your DE estimates are accurate to 3 decimal figures (David Makin in fractalforums.com)

"For exterior distance estimation, you need a large escape radius, eg 100100. Iteration count limit is arbitrary, with a finite limit some pixels will always be classified as "unknown"." Claude Heiland-Allen[\[9\]](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Fractals/Iterations_in_the_complex_plane/demm#cite_note-9)

