## Modifications / optimisations

Creating DEM images can be improved by use of:

- the Koebe 1/4-theorem[\[16\]](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Fractals/Iterations_in_the_complex_plane/demm#cite_note-16)
- gray scale based on distance [\[17\]](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Fractals/Iterations_in_the_complex_plane/demm#cite_note-17)[\[18\]](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Fractals/Iterations_in_the_complex_plane/demm#cite_note-18)
- [Fractal forum: Relationship between bailout and accuracy of analytical DE](http://www.fractalforums.com/programming/relationship-between-bailout-and-accuracy-of-analytical-de/)
- [weight in DEM/M](https://mightymandel.mathr.co.uk/current/usage.html#usageweight)
- if you see double contur of main antenna:

  - increasing resolution does't solve the problem
  - add one pixel to height or change CyMax or CyMin ( add one pixel size).

### equalisation

Distance Estimate Equalisation[\[19\]](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Fractals/Iterations_in_the_complex_plane/demm#cite_note-19)

Program exrdeeq[\[20\]](https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Fractals/Iterations_in_the_complex_plane/demm#cite_note-20)

- reads DEX and DEY channels
- outputs Y channel
- DE less than 0 becomes 0
- DE greater than 1 becomes 1
- otherwise Y is the index of DE in the sorted array, scaled to the range 0 to 1

```
exrdeeq in.exr out.exr
```

